   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the particular solution to the differential equation \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = y\\,(x^{2} - 2x - 3) \\) with the initial condition \\( f(0) = 2 \\). It is known that \\( f(x) > 0 \\) for all \\( x \\)."
   },
   "skills": [
      "BC-SKL-05010",
      "BC-SKL-05020",
      "BC-SKL-05039"
   ],
   "parts": [
      {
         "id": "a",
         "prompt": "Find the \\( x \\)-coordinates of the critical points of \\( f \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "x = -1, \\; x = 3",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Set the derivative equal to zero.",
               "latex": "y\\,(x^{2} - 2x - 3) = 0"
            },
            {
               "text": "Since y = f(x) > 0, only the quadratic factor can vanish.",
               "latex": "(x - 3)(x + 1) = 0, \\quad x = -1, \\; x = 3"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "a1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99013",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-05010"
               ],
               "criterion": "Sets dy/dx = y(x^2 - 2x - 3) equal to zero.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": null
            },
            {
               "point_id": "a2",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-05010"
               ],
               "criterion": "Uses f(x) > 0 to reduce the equation to x^2 - 2x - 3 = 0 and gives both x = -1 and x = 3.",
               "eligible_only_if": [
                  "a1"
               ],
               "check": null
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "b",
         "prompt": "Find \\( \\dfrac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} \\) in terms of \\( x \\) and \\( y \\). Find \\( f''(0) \\), and determine whether the graph of \\( f \\) is concave up or concave down at \\( x = 0 \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "f''(0) = 14, \\text{ concave up}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Product rule, with dy/dx substituted.",
               "latex": "\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} = \\frac{dy}{dx}\\cdot(x^{2} - 2x - 3) + y\\cdot(2x - 2) = y\\cdot(x^{2} - 2x - 3)^{2} + y\\cdot(2x - 2)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate at (0, 2).",
               "latex": "f''(0) = 2(9) + 2(-2) = 14"
            },
            {
               "text": "The second derivative is positive there.",
               "latex": "f''(0) > 0, \\text{ so concave up}"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "b1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-05039"
               ],
               "criterion": "Differentiates with the product rule and substitutes dy/dx, giving y(x^2 - 2x - 3)^2 + y(2x - 2) in any equivalent form in x and y.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": {
                  "kind": "sympy_equivalence",
                  "target": "any_line",
                  "expected": "y*(x**2 - 2*x - 3)**2 + y*(2*x - 2)",
                  "up_to_constant": false,
                  "variable": "x"
               }
            },
            {
               "point_id": "b2",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-05039"
               ],
               "criterion": "Gives f''(0) = 14.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": {
                  "kind": "sympy_equivalence",
                  "target": "any_line",
                  "expected": "14",
                  "up_to_constant": false,
                  "variable": "x"
               }
            },
            {
               "point_id": "b3",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99014",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-05039"
               ],
               "criterion": "States that f''(0) is positive, so the graph of f is concave up at x = 0.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": null,
               "follows_from": [
                  "b2"
               ]
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Use the second derivative test to determine whether \\( f \\) has a relative minimum, a relative maximum, or neither at \\( x = 3 \\). Justify your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\text{relative minimum at } x = 3",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "At x = 3 the factor x^2 - 2x - 3 is zero, so only the second term remains.",
               "latex": "f''(3) = f(3)(2 \\cdot 3 - 2) = 4f(3)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Since f(3) > 0, the second derivative is positive at the critical point.",
               "latex": "f''(3) > 0"
            },
            {
               "text": "Classify.",
               "latex": "\\text{relative minimum at } x = 3"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "c1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99014",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-05039"
               ],
               "criterion": "Shows f''(3) = 4f(3) and states it is positive because f(3) > 0.",
