               "criterion": "Concludes that f has a relative minimum at x = 3, based on f'(3) = 0 and f''(3) > 0.",
               "eligible_only_if": [
                  "c1"
               ],
               "check": null
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Use the first derivative test to determine whether \\( f \\) has a relative minimum, a relative maximum, or neither at \\( x = -1 \\). Justify your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\text{relative maximum at } x = -1",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "The sign of dy/dx is the sign of (x - 3)(x + 1), because y > 0.",
               "latex": "\\operatorname{sign}\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\operatorname{sign}\\bigl((x-3)(x+1)\\bigr)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Just left of x = -1 both factors are negative; just right, only x - 3 is.",
               "latex": "f' > 0 \\text{ on } (-3, -1), \\quad f' < 0 \\text{ on } (-1, 3)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Classify.",
               "latex": "\\text{relative maximum at } x = -1"
            }
